 San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8ee88bfae2173555e65a9071141ab610d6c01f3d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8ee88bfae2173555e65a9071141ab610d6c01f3d.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 15 at 12:00PM MDT until September 18 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River,\nNorthwest San Juan Mountains, San Juan River Basin and Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nThis also includes the Gold Mountain, Elk and Ferris burn scars as\nwell as areas of steep, susceptible terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Recent heavy rainfall in southwest Colorado has led to already\nsaturated ground. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday afternoon through Thursday\nevening producing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cf39aa90455238aaed4fdb23ced03f0914e3184.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cf39aa90455238aaed4fdb23ced03f0914e3184.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-15T19:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 151909 CCA AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion...CORRECTED National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 109 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - There is a chance for strong to severe storms over the nex